<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Buonarroti is an 85-year-old sculptor with hand osteoarthritis, worst at the base of the left thumb, and gout in remission, who came in the same morning after cutting his left index finger. About two hours ago, while roughing out a block, the chisel slipped from his left hand and the edge cut the back of the index finger. He says his pinch grip gave way; he was working without his thumb splint because it was being cleaned. The bleeding stopped with ten minutes of pressure. He can bend and straighten the finger fully and has no numbness. The tools were clean steel; there was marble dust in the wound. He takes no blood thinners. His last tetanus booster was more than ten years ago. He took acetaminophen 1 g for the pain. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mechanism</td><td>Chisel slipped from a weak pinch grip; the splint was off</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>About two hours before the visit</td></tr><tr><td>Bleeding</td><td>Stopped with ten minutes of pressure; no anticoagulant or antiplatelet drug</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Full finger flexion and extension; no numbness</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus status</td><td>Last Tdap more than ten years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Contamination</td><td>Marble dust in the wound; clean steel tool</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

